      "id": "31197910",
      "title": "Improving App Layout & Styling",
      "lectureOrder": 132,
      "videoOrder": 128,
      "sourceHash": "88594bcfce2bdd3d13d6df0942611b93ea725ed99efa6166050c671999c909fe",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.561,
          "end": 4.86,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmuller] So let's now diving into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.86,
          "end": 7.56,
          "en": "styling and creating layouts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.56,
          "end": 10.143,
          "en": "for these different screens and components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.5,
          "end": 13.22,
          "en": "And for this, let's maybe start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.22,
          "end": 15.89,
          "en": "with the Summary component again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.89,
          "end": 19.17,
          "en": "with the ExpensesSummary component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.17,
          "end": 20.81,
          "en": "Now, of course as always,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.81,
          "end": 24.1,
          "en": "the exact layout and styling is always up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.1,
          "end": 26.363,
          "en": "Here's just one suggestion from you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.56,
          "end": 29.61,
          "en": "For this, in the ExpensesSummary component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 33.06,
          "en": "I'll add my styles constant, my styles object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.06,
          "end": 37.06,
          "en": "with help of the StyleSheet object from React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.06,
          "end": 40.1,
          "en": "which therefore must be imported from React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.1,
          "end": 43.593,
          "en": "which we have used many times before in this course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.843,
          "end": 48.21,
          "en": "Through this StyleSheet create method we pass an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.21,
          "end": 51.4,
          "en": "and in this object, we can then define our style object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.4,
          "end": 53.123,
          "en": "with their style properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.15,
          "end": 56.25,
          "en": "And here, I want to set up a general style",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.25,
          "end": 59.81,
          "en": "for this wrapping container, and then a specific style",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.81,
          "end": 62.963,
          "en": "for the period and for the amount, for the sum.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.4,
          "end": 66.85,
          "en": "And for the container, I'll give this style object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.85,
          "end": 68.31,
          "en": "a name of container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.31,
          "end": 70.85,
          "en": "And now here, I think what will look good is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.85,
          "end": 72.95,
          "en": "if we give this a little bit of a padding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.78999999999999,
          "end": 75.96000000000001,
          "en": "then a nice background color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.96000000000001,
          "end": 78.7,
          "en": "to set it apart from the background.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.7,
          "end": 81.293,
          "en": "So from the overall screen background, I mean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.19,
          "end": 84.28999999999999,
          "en": "where I will use my GlobalStyles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.28999999999999,
          "end": 87.51,
          "en": "from this constants styles.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.51,
          "end": 89.78,
          "en": "And for this, the GlobalStyles of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.78,
          "end": 92.09,
          "en": "must be imported like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.09,
          "end": 96.00999999999999,
          "en": "And then with that imported, we can access our colors there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.00999999999999,
          "end": 100.74000000000001,
          "en": "and I want to use primary50 here as a shade,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.74000000000001,
          "end": 103.67,
          "en": "which is a really light purple color,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.67,
          "end": 105.47,
          "en": "because I will later also change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.47,
          "end": 108.06,
          "en": "the overall screen background color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.06,
          "end": 111.25999999999999,
          "en": "And then this light purple background color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.25999999999999,
          "end": 114.67,
          "en": "on the Summary part, in the Summary section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.67,
          "end": 115.86,
          "en": "will look pretty nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.86,
          "end": 118.46000000000001,
          "en": "on that overall darker screen background",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.46000000000001,
          "end": 120.323,
          "en": "which we will add later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.1,
          "end": 124.73,
          "en": "I also think that rounded corners look good,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.73,
          "end": 128.113,
          "en": "so we can add a BorderRadius of six to this container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.12,
          "end": 132.53,
          "en": "and then we wanna manipulate the flex properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.53,
          "end": 136.91,
          "en": "because I want to make sure that the period name and the sum",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.91,
          "end": 140.89,
          "en": "are next to each other and not below each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.89,
          "end": 143.62,
          "en": "For this, we need to switch the flexDirection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.51,
          "end": 147.163,
          "en": "from column, which is the default, to row.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.42000000000002,
          "end": 152.86,
          "en": "And then I wanna have spacing between the two items here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.86,
          "end": 154.49,
          "en": "that are in that row,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.49,
          "end": 157.4,
          "en": "so between the two pieces of text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.4,
          "end": 159.28,
          "en": "And that of course can be achieved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.28,
          "end": 163.09300000000002,
          "en": "with justifyContent space-between.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.09300000000002,
          "end": 166.35,
          "en": "JustifyContent, because with flexDirection row,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.35,
          "end": 168.93,
          "en": "the main access now is left to right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.93,
          "end": 172.373,
          "en": "and justifyContent does target that main access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.49,
          "end": 176.07999999999998,
          "en": "And then I also add alignItems center",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.07999999999998,
          "end": 178.5,
          "en": "to center these two items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.5,
          "end": 181.88,
          "en": "to period name and to sum vertically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.88,
          "end": 184.52,
          "en": "Now we can set up the text specific styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 184.52,
          "end": 188.42,
          "en": "And for this here, I'll set up my period style,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.42,
          "end": 191.74,
          "en": "which will be applied to the period text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.74,
          "end": 194.553,
          "en": "and give this a font size of let's say 12.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.15,
          "end": 201.15,
          "en": "And give it a color of globalStyles.colors.primary400,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 203.11,
          "end": 204.883,
          "en": "which is a darker purple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.23,
          "end": 209.42000000000002,
          "en": "And then I'll add my sum styling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.42000000000002,
          "end": 214.3,
          "en": "where I want to give this a bigger font size of let's say 16",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 214.3,
          "end": 219.3,
          "en": "and a font weight of bold, and then also a color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.2,
          "end": 223.46,
          "en": "And here I'll use almost the same color,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 223.46,
          "end": 227.423,
          "en": "but I'll use a slightly darker purple with the 500 shade.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.87,
          "end": 230.36,
          "en": "Now, as a little side note,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 230.36,
          "end": 234.06,
          "en": "here in this app, I'm using the default system fonts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.06,
          "end": 236.57999999999998,
          "en": "You could of course also set up custom fonts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.57999999999998,
          "end": 239.02,
          "en": "as you learned it earlier in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.02,
          "end": 241.42,
          "en": "Here, because I like those default fonts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 241.42,
          "end": 242.563,
          "en": "I will stick to them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.41,
          "end": 248.03,
          "en": "Now we set up all these styling objects in our StyleSheet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.03,
          "end": 253.03,
          "en": "Now we can apply them to our elements here, to our JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 253.15,
          "end": 255.62,
          "en": "And the outer view should receive the container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 255.62,
          "end": 259.053,
          "en": "so we add the style prop and then add styles.container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.96,
          "end": 261.89,
          "en": "And this period text will receive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 261.89,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "the styles.period styling object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 270.2,
          "en": "And the sum, the amount text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.2,
          "end": 275.2,
          "en": "will receive the styles.sum styling object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 277.22,
          "end": 280.7,
          "en": "With all of that done, if you save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 280.7,
          "end": 282.9,
          "en": "this is how it should look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.9,
          "end": 285.04,
          "en": "That is not the final style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.04,
          "end": 286.83,
          "en": "This is just an intermediate style,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 286.83,
          "end": 288.453,
          "en": "but it doesn't look too bad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 289.47,
          "end": 291.01,
          "en": "Now it will look much better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 291.01,
          "end": 295.09000000000003,
          "en": "as soon as we change the overall screen background.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.09000000000003,
          "end": 298.62,
          "en": "And for this we can go to the ExpensesOutput component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 298.62,
          "end": 300.81,
          "en": "because that will hold the summary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 300.81,
          "end": 304.46,
          "en": "and that is the main component that is returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 304.46,
          "end": 309.45,
          "en": "by both the AlExpenses and RecentExpenses screen components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 309.45,
          "end": 311.43,
          "en": "So if we change these styling here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 311.43,
          "end": 313.593,
          "en": "we will affect those two screens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 314.73,
          "end": 316.21,
          "en": "Now we do have a wrapping view",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 316.21,
          "end": 319.66,
          "en": "around our summary and list here, and we can use this view",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 319.66,
          "end": 322.3,
          "en": "to manipulate the style of the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 322.3,
          "end": 324.83,
          "en": "the background of the screen for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 325.78,
          "end": 328.55,
          "en": "For this, we cannot also add our styles object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 328.55,
          "end": 331.88,
          "en": "with StyleSheet, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 331.88,
          "end": 334.523,
          "en": "imported from React Native as always.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 335.83,
          "end": 338.89,
          "en": "And then on StyleSheet as always, we call create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 338.89,
          "end": 342.103,
          "en": "and pass an object to it, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 343.31,
          "end": 345.49,
          "en": "And then in this object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 345.49,
          "end": 347.8,
          "en": "I will set up another container style",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 347.8,
          "end": 351.82,
          "en": "for this view that wraps the summary and the list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 351.82,
          "end": 354.36,
          "en": "And here are on this container style,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 354.36,
          "end": 356.61,
          "en": "I want to add a lot of padding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 356.61,
          "end": 359.72,
          "en": "let's say 24 pixels, and a background color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 359.72,
          "end": 362.51,
          "en": "which will therefore be the main background color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 362.51,
          "end": 363.863,
          "en": "of this screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 365.14,
          "end": 367.666,
          "en": "And here I'll also use my GlobalStyles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 367.666,
          "end": 369.74,
          "en": "and therefore just as many times before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 369.74,
          "end": 373.92,
          "en": "you of course also must import those GlobalStyles here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 373.92,
          "end": 378.41,
          "en": "You must add this import in ExpensesOutput.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 378.41,
          "end": 381.173,
          "en": "as we did it in other component files as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 382.22,
          "end": 386.27,
          "en": "And then here we can access GlobalStyle.colors.primary700.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 389.09,
          "end": 393.13,
          "en": "Now we can apply our container style to this view",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 393.13,
          "end": 396.323,
          "en": "by setting the style property to styles.container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 397.29,
          "end": 399.33,
          "en": "And if we do that and this by the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 399.33,
          "end": 400.95,
          "en": "is a very dark purple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 400.95,
          "end": 404.33299999999997,
          "en": "If you check the colors here, it's a very dark purple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 405.19,
          "end": 407.51,
          "en": "If we do all of that and we save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 407.51,
          "end": 409.293,
          "en": "now we got this background color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 410.65999999999997,
          "end": 412.43,
          "en": "Now we also see the padding in effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 412.43,
          "end": 413.623,
          "en": "and this looks better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 414.58,
          "end": 417.35,
          "en": "Now of course, what would also look pretty good",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 417.35,
          "end": 421.363,
          "en": "is if this would take up the entire available screen estate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 422.26,
          "end": 423.87,
          "en": "And that of course can be achieved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
